,title,link,text,language,family
0,Ossetian language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ossetian_language,"The Ossetian language belongs to the Iranian group of the Indo-European family of languages (as hinted by its endonym: ирон, irōn). Within Iranian, it is placed in the Eastern subgroup and further to a Northeastern sub-subgroup, but these are areal rather than genetic groups.",Ossetic,Indo-European
1,Music of Ossetia - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_Ossetia,Ossetia is a region located on both sides of the Greater Caucasus Mountains. The folk music of Ossetia (Iron Ossetic: Ирыстоны музыкæ/Irystony musykæ) began to be collected and recorded in the late 19th and early 20th century.,Ossetic,Indo-European
2,Ossetia - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ossetia,The Ossetian language is part of the Eastern Iranian branch of the family of Indo-European languages.[1] Most countries recognize the Ossetian-speaking area south of the main Caucasus ridge as lying within the borders of Georgia...,Ossetic,Indo-European
3,Autumn Songs Of The Ossetic Folk Calendar: On Typology And ...,https://www.europeanproceedings.com/article/10.15405/epsbs.2021.05.58,"The musical folklore of the Ossetic folk calendar is evaluated through an integrated approach that exposes an integral and systemic nature of calendar rituals, which is also facilitated by the findings in related sciences (ethnolinguistics, philological folklore, ethnography, etc.).",Ossetic,Indo-European
4,Ossetic Language - (CAIS),http://www.cais-soas.com/CAIS/Languages/ossetic.htm,"The phonology of the language has been greatly influenced by the non-Indo-European languages of the Caucasus, and the present vocabulary has many loanwords from Russian. There are many folk epics in Ossetic; the most famous are the tales about hero warriors, the Narts.",Ossetic,Indo-European
5,The Sound of Indo-European Music (Compilation) - YouTube,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WgHSW774Q-4,"Sep 8, 2019 · In this video, I compiled music from all the major Indo-European languages. I hope you enjoy these great songs!",Ossetic,Indo-European
6,"Indo-European languages | Family, Map, Characteristics... | Britannica",https://www.britannica.com/topic/Indo-European-languages,"Indo-European languages are a family of languages spoken in most of Europe and areas of European settlement and in much of Southwest and South Asia. The 10 main branches of the family are Anatolian, Indo-Iranian, Greek, Italic, Germanic, Armenian, Tocharian, Celtic...",Ossetic,Indo-European
7,Non-verbal predication in Ossetic,https://indo-iranian.org/iil/article/download/7/8/182,"Ossetic is an Iranian Indo-European language spoken by up to 614,000 speakers, according to the Ethnologue,1 in the Northern Cau-casus and other areas. The most important dialectal split is between the Iron and Digor varieties.",Ossetic,Indo-European
8,GitHub - timarkh/uniparser-grammar-ossetic: Morphological analysis...,https://github.com/timarkh/uniparser-grammar-ossetic,"It is based on a formalized description of the morphology of literary Ossetic, which is based on the Iron dialect, and uses uniparser-morph for parsing. It performs full morphological analysis of Ossetic words (lemmatization, POS tagging, grammatical tagging). How to use. Python package.",Ossetic,Indo-European
